{% extends "layouts/base" %}
{% set title = "Islands" %}
{% set name = visitor() %}

{% block content %}
	<h1>Server islands playground</h1>
	<p>The same product page, with three islands, rendered three ways:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="/static/">Static build</a>: built once by <code>npm run build</code> with <code>deferIslands</code>. Each island fetches its HTML from <code>/_islands/:id</code>.</li>
		<li><a href="/stream/">Streamed</a>: rendered for each request with <code>renderStream</code> and <code>streamIslands</code>. Islands follow the page in the same response, in the order they finish. <a href="/stream/?fail">Make the reviews island fail</a>.</li>
		<li><a href="/in-place/">In place</a>: <code>render</code> with no option, so nothing arrives until the slowest island is done.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Visitor</h2>
	{% if name %}
		<p>Signed in as {{ name }}. <a href="/sign-out">Sign out</a></p>
	{% else %}
		<form action="/sign-in">
			<label>Name <input name="name" required></label>
			<button>Sign in</button>
		</form>
	{% endif %}
	<p class="meta">The basket island reads this cookie in its own request, even on the static page.</p>
{% endblock %}
